*   **At $x1 \approx 15$ (around $t \approx 4.1$s):** As the value decreases, 
there is another abrupt change in curvature. The rate of descent changes 
(becoming less steep) as the system switches back into the mode that handles the
"trough" behavior.

These points—at approximately **$x1 = 25$** and **$x1 = 15$**—represent the 
guard conditions or switching thresholds between the two discrete states of the 
hybrid system. One mode appears to be active when the value is within the 
"middle" range, and the other mode takes over to push the value back toward the 
center once it hits these outer boundaries.
