The system behaves like a damped oscillator where the damping coefficient ($a$) 
changes depending on the direction of motion. This is a common model for systems
with asymmetric friction or directional damping mechanisms. The stability of    
both modes is evident as $b < 0$ and $a < 0$, leading to a stable equilibrium at
$x_1 = 0$.                                                                      
